  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Deal** (1 review): Reviewer calls the Deal blistering, with John burning on the set-one closer [7]\n- **Days Between** (1 review): Reviewer says the band takes this song to an almost orchestral new level [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **dc2017-11-21** (recommended): source not stated; 16 songs; 164 min; rated 3.6/5 by 5 [1]. Said about its sound: On an iPod the tracks have audible gaps between them, though iTunes playback doesn't show them [6]\n- **DeadCo2017-11-21.travitz.schoepsMK4v.flac16**: source not stated; 16 songs; 165 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer ranks this among the best Dead and Company shows ever, musically [6]\n- Reviewer says this Deal matches the set-one-ending Deals the band plays on every tour [7]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **dc2017-11-21**: taped by Alex Leary; transferred by Alex Leary; source: DPA 4023 > Sound Devices MixPre-6 (24/48) [1]\n- **DeadCo2017-11-21.travitz.schoepsMK4v.flac16**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps MK4V's>KCY>VMS5u>SD744t [2]. Also: Taped with Schoeps MK4V microphones through Schoeps KCY and VMS02ib preamps into a Sound Devices 744t recorder; Edited in Sound Forge Pro 11 for fades, tracked in CDWAV, converted to FLAC with Trader's Little Helper, tagged in Foobar2000 [2]",
